From 9abff68b358223a4fb4567195109d6c67d0492a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:58:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: version of the data structures exported by
 the libraries

`MFRONT_GPB_API_VERSION`, defined in
`MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/BatchData.h`, gives the version of the
data structures exchanged with the generated functions. The libraries of
behaviours and models export it (`<name>_generic_parallel_api_version`),
so that the calling code can check that it uses the same structures. The
backend writes this symbol and the name of the backend for both
interfaces.

The documentation explains why the error messages of the points are not
reported, and how to obtain them with the `generic` interface.
