diff --git a/docs/web/generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.md b/docs/web/generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.md
index b64c573e5..1b639e4cb 100644
--- a/docs/web/generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.md
+++ b/docs/web/generic-parallel-behaviour-interface.md
@@ -107,7 +107,11 @@ which tells the calling code where the fields must be allocated (see the
 section of each backend).
 
 The data structures are declared in
-`MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/BatchData.h`.
+`MFront/GenericParallelBehaviour/BatchData.h`. Their version is given by the
+`MFRONT_GPB_API_VERSION` macro, incremented at each incompatible change, and
+exported by the libraries (`generic_parallel_api_version` symbol, an
+`unsigned short`), so that the calling code can check that it uses the same
+structures.
 
 ## Fields
 
@@ -225,6 +229,14 @@ The status, also returned by the function, is:
 - `-3` in case of a runtime error of the backend (allocation, launch of a
   kernel, etc.).
 
+The message describes invalid arguments and runtime errors. The error
+messages of the points (`error_message` of the `generic` interface) are not
+reported: the code executed on a device can't throw exceptions, and a
+buffer per point would increase the stack of the threads. The `statuses`
+field locates the points where the integration failed: the error message of
+such a point can be obtained by integrating it with the `generic`
+interface.
+
 ## Execution options
 
